# HQL-0064: Processes: `io.process`, child processes, pipes, `parallel` and watchdogs

**Status**: drafted
**Created**: 2026-11-22
**Source**: design discussion of 2026-11-22 on [[HQL-0062]]: a script that
reads its arguments and reports an exit status also needs to start other
programs, talk to them and run two things at once

!!! warning "Design only"
    Nothing in this proposal is implemented. Every part is a design
    direction for discussion.

## Abstract

A script is a Unix process. [[HQL-0062]] makes an HQL file runnable as one
and gives it its arguments and its exit status. This proposal gives it the
rest of the process model: its identifier and its signals, in a module
`io.process`; child processes, as an endpoint `command(program, args)` read
and written by `source`, `tap`, `target` and `sink`; named pipes, as an
endpoint `fifo(name)` of `io.fs`; the keyword `parallel`, which runs
branches at the same time and joins them; and watchdogs, which ask a child
a question at an interval.

Every operation follows the rules of the note
[pure and effectful](../HQL-0062/parts/01-pure-and-effectful.hmd) of
[[HQL-0062]]: an effect is declared `effectful`, returns an ordinary value,
gives a handleable failure as a `Result`, and never ends the process.

## Motivation

- A script cannot run another program. A shell pipeline can call `git`,
  `kubectl` or `sort`; an HQL script can only be one stage of such a
  pipeline, fed by a shell around it.
- A script cannot stop cleanly on `SIGTERM`, and cannot signal another
  process.
- A script cannot read a named pipe: `File` is `Replayable`, and a pipe is
  not.
- HQL evaluates statements in order. A program that writes to a child while
  it reads the child's answers has no way to say so.
- A child that is running and no longer answers cannot be told from one that
  works. In ETL this is the common fault: a stage that consumes a streaming
  queue never ends by design, so only its measurements show that it has
  hung or stopped giving output.

## The parts

| Part | Defines |
| --- | --- |
| [`io.process`](parts/01-io-process.hmd) | the Unix process model against HQL, the module `io.process`, `Signal`, `signals` and `send`, the `process` grant, and signals on Windows |
| [child processes](parts/02-child-processes.hmd) | `command` against Python's `subprocess`, Haskell's `System.Process` and Rust's `Command`; the five operations; a child's three pipes; failures; text that is not UTF-8; process groups and lifetime; the `commands` grant; Windows, its Job Objects and `crates/hql-sys` |
| [advanced child processes](parts/03-advanced-child-processes.hmd) | a child's pipes wired to channels: `stdin_from`, `stdout_to`, `stderr_to`, and `command(…).stderr` |
| [named pipes](parts/04-named-pipes.hmd) | `fifo(name)` and `fifo(path)` in `io.fs`, a named pipe handed to a child, and Windows named pipes |
| [`parallel`](parts/05-parallel.hmd) | the keyword `parallel`: the block, the step, `join = any`, branches against children, and how it runs |
| [watchdogs](parts/06-watchdog.hmd) | `Watchdog`, a question asked of a child or a block at an interval; a side note on `io.process.monitoring`, measurements, idle and reports |
| [boilerplate logging](parts/07-boilerplate-logging.hmd) | the use case, an unhealthy consumer of a streaming queue; who takes a `Measurement` and how it reaches a watchdog; children's standard error, reports and measurements in channels; the wiring written once; logical zombies, certain as `deadlock` and suspected as idle |
| [I/O FAQ](parts/faq.hmd) | the programs that hang, fail or surprise under these rules, those that read as a mistake and are correct, and those that behave differently on Windows |

## Relation to other proposals

- [[HQL-0062]] keeps `#!`, `hql FILE`, positional arguments, `io.env.argv()`
  and the exit status. `argv` stays in `io.env`, beside `arg` and `args`.
- [[HQL-0055]] states which effects are ordered and which rewrites a planner
  may make. `parallel` changes one rule: effects of two branches are
  unordered.
- [[HQL-0033]]: a non-zero exit status of a child is an `err` under `run`.
- [[HQL-0059]] holds the configuration keys that the grants `process` and
  `commands` would add.
- [[0083-io-programs-that-never-end|Issue 0083]] collects every way an I/O
  program can wait without end.

